    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'bother' is a verb. The Japanese expression '迷惑' (meiwaku) is primarily a noun meaning 'trouble, bother, annoyance, nuisance, inconvenience.' It is not a standalone verb. To express the verb 'bother,' it typically combines with する (suru) to form '迷惑する' (to be bothered/troubled, intransitive) or '迷惑をかける' (to cause bother/trouble, transitive). The assigned POS for '迷惑' as a verb is incorrect, leading to a grammatical and semantic mismatch for a verb-to-verb alignment. A learner would not use '迷惑' as a verb.",
