      "reading": "めいわくする",
      "reason": "This is a correct and natural verbal form (intransitive) for 'to be bothered/troubled,' directly aligning with Sense 1 of the JMdict entry for 迷惑 ('to be troubled (by), to be bothered (by)'). For the transitive sense 'to bother someone,' '迷惑をかける' would be appropriate, but '迷惑する' covers a common aspect of the verb 'bother' and is derived directly from the noun '迷惑'."
